cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Postnet-CF: Federated LLM gate-controller training across browser tabs with verified byzantine defense"
message: "If you use this software or refer to the protocol, please cite the Zenodo archive."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ahmet Barış
    family-names: Günaydın
    email: abgunaydin94@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/abgnydn/postnet-cf"
url: "https://postnet-cf.abgunaydin94.workers.dev"
version: "0.6"
abstract: >
  A federated learning protocol whose workers are unmodified browser tabs and
  whose coordinator is a Cloudflare Durable Object. Updates are single-scalar
  SPSA estimates with a 20-byte wire format independent of model size after
  bootstrap. Includes federated training of NTK-Mirror gate controllers on a
  frozen Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct, with a hardened byzantine defense
  (no-self-audit cross-rotation + magnitude-lie test) validated across 5
  random seeds at an attacker fraud-detection rate of 1.000 ± 0.000.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - SPSA
  - DeComFL
  - NTK-Mirror
  - Cloudflare Workers
  - byzantine fault tolerance
  - browser-tab swarm
  - large language models
  - Qwen
license: MIT
